<title>BULGARIA: Iraq oil contract approved with Bulgaria Himimport.</title>
<headline>Iraq oil contract approved with Bulgaria Himimport.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's chemical and oil trading firm Himimport said on Wednesday the United Nations had approved its 15,000 barrels per day sales contract with Iraq.</p>
<p>Himimport's deputy general director Sasho Stoyanov said his firm signed a six-month contract on December 11 with Iraq's State Oil Marketing Organisation (SOMO) to purchase crude under the U.N. approved oil-for-food deal.</p>
<p>&quot;Bulgaria's Neftihim oil refinery will refine the Iraqi crude,&quot; Stoyanov told Reuters.</p>
<p>Under the U.N. deal Iraq is allowed to export $2 billion of its oil over six months to pay for much-needed humanitarian supplies after six years of crippling international sanctions following its invasion of Kuwait.</p>
<p>-- Liliana Semerdjieva, Sofia Newsroom +359 2 84561</p>
